  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>A) Phenol reacts with chloroform in presence of aqueous sodium hydroxide to form salicylaldehyde, which is named as&nbsp;Riemer-Tiemann reaction.</p><p>B)Phenol when heated with zinc dust forms benzene.</p><p>C)Oxidation of phenol with acidified potassium dichromate gives benzoquinone.</p><p>D)&nbsp;Bromination of phenol in presence of&nbsp;a&nbsp;non-polar solvent like CS<sub>2</sub>&nbsp;gives para-bromo phenol as the major product.</p><p>(A)&nbsp;<img src=\"assets\\st0089_bac3a9c070e4.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 106px;\" /></p><p>(B)</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0089_09d1766b660e.png\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 126px;\" /></p><p>(C)&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0089_1fcf2cf80921.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 131px;\" /></p><p>(D)</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0089_7e2ef26bfe16.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 141px;\" /></p>"
